  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14133305/assets/b8fb2d8be9596083481f83e6c8bacbb6a988ad527ef0a468583c239ea5e43838.png)\n\nWhat ratio describes the number of triangles to the total number of shapes?",
  "worked_solution": "We can express the ratio of the number of triangles to the total number of shapes as follows:\n\n$$\n\\text{number of triangles}:\\text{total number of shapes}\n$$\n\nTo find this ratio, we start by counting the number of occurrences of each shape:\n\n- First, we count the number of triangles. There are $2$ triangles.\n\n- Next, we count the total number of shapes. There are $7$ shapes.\n\nTherefore, the ratio of triangles to total shapes is $2:7.$",
